Pass the thinking switch (reasoningEffort) through the developer chat routes.

Why: the Ollama provider sends think false when a chat carries reasoningEffort off
(server/utils/helpers/reasoningEffort.js), but only the session-auth UI routes
(server/endpoints/chat.js) read reasoningEffort. The /api/v1 workspace and thread chat and
stream-chat routes, which the AskFiles search page uses, never pass it to
server/utils/chats/apiChatHandler.js, so qwen3 answers always start with a think block. The four
routes now read reasoningEffort from the request body; apiChatHandler falls back to the
environment variable DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT and resolves it against the model's capabilities
the same way the UI path does (server/utils/chats/stream.js). The AskFiles presets set
DEFAULT_REASONING_EFFORT=off.

Paths are relative to upstream/. Apply from the repository root with
  git apply --directory=upstream patches/007-reasoning-effort-api.patch

